; Regression test for issue #3281: `--empty` combined with an `account`
; directive failed with "Too few arguments to function" when the --limit
; predicate tested a property of the posting, as in
; `bal --empty -l 'commodity !~ /GBP/'`.
;
; With --empty, the balance report (#1204) and the accounts listing also
; admit accounts that were declared but never used.  To honour the query
; (#3189, #3212), each such account was checked by evaluating the whole
; --limit predicate against the account itself.  But --limit is a posting
; predicate: only the account terms (`account`, `account_base`, `depth`)
; mean the same thing for an account.  Every other name either failed to
; evaluate (`commodity`, `cost`, and `code` -- produced by the `#CODE` query
; syntax) or quietly tested something unrelated: `date` became the
; account's latest posting date, so `-b` hid declared accounts while `-e`
; showed them.
;
; A declared account that no posting in the report reaches is now kept
; unless the account terms of the predicate rule it out.  Terms about a
; posting cannot be judged for an account without one, so they neither
; exclude it nor raise an error.

account Assets:Savings
account Equity:Opening balance

2022-01-11 * (101) Monthly fee
    Expenses:Fees                5.00 GBP
    Assets:Pension              -5.00 GBP

2022-02-11 * Monthly fee
    Expenses:Fees                5.00 GBP
    Assets:Pension              -5.00 GBP

; The command from the issue report.  Every posting is in GBP, so only the
; declared accounts remain.
test --empty bal -l 'commodity !~ /GBP/'
                   0  Assets:Savings
                   0  Equity:Opening balance
--------------------
                   0
end test

; The second command from the issue report.
test --empty bal --pivot Fund -l 'commodity !~ /GBP/'
                   0  Assets:Savings
                   0  Equity:Opening balance
--------------------
                   0
end test

; The accounts listing admits declared accounts the same way (#3212).
test accounts -l 'commodity !~ /GBP/'
Assets:Savings
Equity:Opening balance
end test

; The account term still filters declared accounts, even though the
; posting term is evaluated first: Equity is ruled out by `Assets`.
test --empty bal -l 'commodity !~ /GBP/' Assets
                   0  Assets:Savings
end test

; A code query (`#CODE`) used to fail with "Unknown identifier 'code'".
test --empty bal '#101'
           -5.00 GBP  Assets
           -5.00 GBP    Pension
                   0    Savings
                   0  Equity:Opening balance
            5.00 GBP  Expenses:Fees
--------------------
                   0
end test

; A begin date used to hide declared accounts, while an end date did not.
test --empty bal -b 2022-02-01
           -5.00 GBP  Assets
           -5.00 GBP    Pension
                   0    Savings
                   0  Equity:Opening balance
            5.00 GBP  Expenses:Fees
--------------------
                   0
end test

test --empty bal -e 2022-02-01
           -5.00 GBP  Assets
           -5.00 GBP    Pension
                   0    Savings
                   0  Equity:Opening balance
            5.00 GBP  Expenses:Fees
--------------------
                   0
end test
